Records the owner's ruling of 2026-08-27 on WI-gohok, put as three options and
answered B.

THE PROBLEM. Measurement 0005 surfaced a limit that is not a bug in any
producer: the taint model, and every precision rubric to date, cannot separate a
value that LEAKS from one a config-driven program was TOLD to act on. caddy
reads its config from stdin; the config names a log file; the bytes reach
os.Chmod through a chain citable in caddy's own source. Under the 0001 rubric
that is a TRUE POSITIVE -- an independent adjudication commissioned for this
exact question agreed and accepted the consequence: every filesystem, network
and subprocess operation whose argument comes from a configured value is a true
positive, for any config-driven server. True and uninformative at once, over a
class that is every config field of every module in a plugin-registry
architecture.

WHY IT GATED THE BASELINE. The standing decision band is denominated in
usefulness ("<=25% useful => recall stays stopped") while the instrument
computes only correctness -- 0006 itself calls 33.9% "an upper bound on useful
precision, not a measure of it". A series would have tracked correctness for
months without answering the question the band exists to answer. INV-duvup
requires the rubric fixed IN ADVANCE, so this had to land before the first
datum.

THE RULING. Correctness precision is unchanged (TP / adjudicated), so 0001's
"exploitability is not the question" is not relitigated and comparability with
0001-0006 is preserved by construction. Useful precision is published alongside
as (TP - VACUOUS) / adjudicated -- same denominator, numerator-only deduction,
so useful <= correctness always.

THE AMENDMENT THAT KEEPS IT OBJECTIVE. The exclusion is STRUCTURAL, not a
severity judgement; adjudication objectivity is what produced 94.6% independent
panel agreement on 0006. A finding is CONFIGURED-ACTION only when three things
are each CITABLE: a declared-configuration source, a deserialization into a
declared configuration schema, and a sink argument read from a field of that
schema which the sink operation exists to consume. Any clause that cannot be
cited leaves the finding counted as useful, so the test can only UNDERSTATE the
damage.

TWO VACUITY CLASSES, REPORTED SEPARATELY because they have opposite lifetimes.
CONFIGURED-ACTION is a permanent model limit. KIND-MISDECLARED (a Haskell IORef
filed under untrusted-input-no-database) is a DEFECT -- INV-nular -- that gets
fixed, not excluded. Conflating them would launder a bug through a rubric
change.

A PROVENANCE GAP THIS DOES NOT PAPER OVER. The measurements index publishes
0006's useful precision as <=25.0%, which requires removing TEN of 38 TPs; the
record names FIVE (all of shellcheck's). The figure may be right -- section A
tabulates kind-misdeclarations in five languages -- but it is not derivable from
the record, and it is the number a program-level band is written against. Filed
as WI-gibom, which now blocks INV-duvup; the ADR states it is not carried
forward on authority.

